<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's Cisneros to open brewery in 1997.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's Cisneros to open brewery in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan holding company Grupo Cisneros expects to open a new brewery in April 1997 to capture some 10 percent of the 16 million litres per year local beer market, the company said.</p>
<p>With an expected upfront investment of some $210 million &quot;we're currently talking to four or five potential partners,&quot; Oswaldo Cisneros, one of the powerful private company's directors, told reporters.</p>
<p>An agreement will be announced over the next couple of months and the beer will be called &quot;Fria&quot;, he added.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
